articles.content_en:
Citizens and organizations shall perform the following obligations to safeguard national security:
(1) Abide by the relevant provisions of the Constitution, laws, and regulations concerning national security;
(2) Promptly report clues concerning activities that endanger national security;
(3) Truthfully provide evidence that they know of concerning activities that endanger national security;
(4) Provide convenient conditions or other assistance for national security work;
(5) Provide necessary support and assistance to the State security organs, public security organs, and relevant military organs;
(6) Keep confidential State secrets that they know of;
(7) Other obligations prescribed by laws and administrative regulations.
No individual or organization may engage in acts endangering national security, nor provide any financial support or assistance to any individual or organization endangering national security.
